From 446c55a98e3e4930dfa7699bb37bc3466f04982b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:17:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] audio: drop the duplicate bluetooth.audio VINTF fragment from
 the APEX

A full build failed at checkvintf with a fatal duplicate:

  VINTF parse error: Conflicting FqInstance:
    IBluetoothAudioProviderFactory/default (@6)
    from /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/bluetooth_audio.xml vs.
    from /apex/com.android.hardware.audio/.../android.hardware.bluetooth.audio.xml
  ERROR: Cannot fetch vendor manifest.

android.hardware.bluetooth.audio is declared twice: the base product
(inherited) installs the standalone android.hardware.bluetooth.audio-impl
with its bluetooth_audio.xml vintf fragment into /vendor, and this APEX
also bundles the identical manifest as a prebuilt. The APEX's audio
service already links the impl and registers the factory, so the running
provider is the APEX either way; the two manifests are byte-identical
(same interface, version 6, same fqname). Drop the APEX's copy so the
device declares the HAL exactly once. The standalone /vendor manifest
remains and the APEX service continues to serve it.

Latent until now: it only fires when the APEX is reassembled, which this
device had not done since the manifests diverged. It blocks every image
build regardless of the change that triggers the reassembly.

Change-Id: Ib841bd951fb37cc12432e513ed484aef1f3ca396
---
 audio/aidl/default/apex/com.android.hardware.audio/Android.bp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/apex/com.android.hardware.audio/Android.bp b/audio/aidl/default/apex/com.android.hardware.audio/Android.bp
index 510fee5f84..e1353e3361 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/apex/com.android.hardware.audio/Android.bp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/apex/com.android.hardware.audio/Android.bp
@@ -47,7 +47,6 @@ apex {
     prebuilts: [
         "android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.example.rc",
         "android.hardware.audio.service-aidl.xml",
-        "android.hardware.bluetooth.audio.xml",
         "audio_eraser_classifier_model",
         "audio_eraser_separator_model",
     ],
-- 
2.43.0

